  "answer": "The bias-variance tradeoff is a fundamental principle in machine learning that describes the relationship between the complexity of a model and its performance on a given task. As the model's complexity increases, its performance tends to improve, but at the cost of increased bias and decreased variance. In simpler terms, as the model becomes more complex, it becomes more likely to make mistakes, but it also becomes more accurate. This tradeoff is a key consideration in the development of machine learning algorithms, as it allows for a balance between model complexity and model interpretability.",
  "confidence": "high",
